<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese groups study forming telecom operator.</title>
<headline>Portuguese groups study forming telecom operator.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity distributor EDP is studying the possibility of forming a telecommunications group in Portugal in partnership with mobile phone operator Telecel and gas company Transgas, an EDP spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The project to establish a second fixed telecommunications network is being studied,&quot; Antonio Ribeiro dos Santos, spokesman of EDP-Electricidade de Portugal, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said no formal timetable had been set.</p>
<p>The dominant telecommunications operator in Portugal is Portugal Telecom.</p>
<p>-- David Brough, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
